{"The new denial-cache precedence test claims permCache allows access but actually sets the permission to false, so it would deny even if permDenialCache were ignored, potentially masking regressions": 0.7777337431907654, "The denial-cache key concatenates components with '_' delimiters even though Grafana UIDs can contain underscores, allowing different (name,parent) pairs to map to the same key and cause incorrect authorization denials for unrelated resources": 0.7997334599494934, "A denial-cache hit returns an immediate deny without re-checking cached permissions or re-querying the DB, which can delay newly granted access to a resource until the denial TTL expires": 0.7981715798377991}